- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests`

**How to implement.** The Materials window opens Online sources, and what a pull adds shows in it at once (001 §O; the S13.1 brief 'Materials window: an Online sources... search and fetch UI'; .spec-md §10.1 discoverability, §10.4 completion refresh; 001 §P: the button and the test send the same message). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`: (a) `MaterialsWindowContext` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:154`, steps 109, 110) gains `openOnlineSources : unit -> unit`, documented in one line: opens the single-instance Online sources window over the context's import seam (the composition root bakes it; tests record). (b) `MaterialsWindowMsg` gains `OpenOnlineSources`, documented in one line. (c) `updateMaterialsWindow`: `OpenOnlineSources` calls `context.openOnlineSources ()` and answers the model unchanged. (d) The verbs row (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:verbsRow`), in Browse mode and after step 119's export verbs: while `context.catalogueImports.materialSources` (step 444) is not empty, `verbButton ConstructorUiId.materialsOnlineSourcesButton (ControlCaption "Online sources…") (fun () -> dispatch OpenOnlineSources)`. Select mode never shows it, because a pick session imports nothing. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindow.fs`: the context's `openOnlineSources` is `openBrowse WindowLauncher.MaterialSourcesWindowKey (fun () -> MaterialSourcesWindow(catalogueImports, fun summary -> dispatch (MaterialsWindowView.MaterialsImportApplied summary)) :> Window)` (steps 110, 451), so a pull's or an update's caption becomes the window's import status and its next render re-queries the store, listing the pulled material and its new versions with no reload. The class doc names Online sources in no more words. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Materials window group (`UiIds.fs:525`): `materialsOnlineSourcesButton` (`"MaterialsOnlineSourcesButton"`) under a one-line comment citing spec 0050 S13.1. (4) Tests, in `MaterialsWindowTests`: `stubContext` (steps 110, 119) passes a recording `openOnlineSources`. `the Online sources UiId of the Materials window is the stable intent-named id`. `Online sources… is offered in Browse mode while the import seam carries a source`: over an import context whose `materialSources` holds step 443's double, the Browse view shows `materialsOnlineSourcesButton`, and `OpenOnlineSources` records one open and answers the model unchanged; over `[]`, and in Select mode, the button is absent. `a pull's caption is the Materials window's status and the pulled material is listed`: after the double's Silicon record is pulled through the context's import seam (`pullRecord`, step 444), `MaterialsImportApplied` of its caption sets `importStatus` to it, and `filteredEntries` lists the pulled material. With trait `ui-smoke`: `acceptance: Online sources… opens one Online sources window over the app's refractiveindex.info source`: over `AppContext.create (TestAppScope.fileLocations (FolderName "MaterialsWindowTests")) WorkbenchSettings.defaults` (steps 88, 446), a `MaterialsWindow` built as the launcher builds it (`ctx.materials`, `ctx.categories`, `ctx.catalogueImports`) is shown headless; pressing `materialsOnlineSourcesButton` opens exactly one `MaterialSourcesWindow`, observed through `Window.WindowOpenedEvent` as `LauncherTests.clickAndObserve` observes, whose `materialSourceChoice` names `refractiveindex.info` and whose `materialSourceSnapshotText` reads `No snapshot yet; Update snapshot downloads the database.`; pressing it again opens no second window. Nothing presses Update snapshot, so nothing is downloaded.

**Acceptance.** After the button is wired, the Materials window MUST offer `Online sources…` in Browse mode while its import seam carries a source, `OpenOnlineSources` MUST open the single-instance Online sources window, and a pull's caption MUST become its import status; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: Online sources… opens one Online sources window over the app's refractiveindex.info source`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Online sources UiId of the Materials window is the stable intent-named id`, `Online sources… is offered in Browse mode while the import seam carries a source` and `a pull's caption is the Materials window's status and the pulled material is listed`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
